IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wcima-compensation`

-- Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023 (WA) and its Regulations 2024, ss 6, 12, 13, 17-20, 25, 28, 29, 36, 47, 48, 51, 55-57, 69-78, 97-101, 186, 202, 204, 215, 415-424, 434; regs 4, 13-18, 23, 24, 90, 122, 134 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case. The regulations used are the deposited Regulations 2024 (mrdoc 49606).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_workers-compensation-and-injury-management-act-2023_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Life facts used (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-jake and -daniel, facts.json): Jake rides for a delivery
-- platform on an ABN as a sole trader; on 12 April 2029 a car door breaks his wrist on a delivery (k044). Employed by
-- Sentinel Security Services from 2034, he falls on a wet stairwell on patrol in the tower where Jarrah is a tenant on
-- 5 October 2053, is off eleven weeks and is assessed at 14% whole person impairment (k085; d080 from the tenant's side).
-- Jarrah takes on three employees on 1 June 2031 (d044). The scenarios give no earnings, claim dates or index figures:
-- the $1,500 pre-injury weekly rate, the ABS earnings and WPI changes, the claim dates and the $252,724 general maximum
-- amount used for the limits (the reg 134 starting figure, unvaried) are ILLUSTRATIVE. Whether Jake's riding was a business
-- he regularly carried on in his own name (s 12(2)(c)(i)) is not stated: both answers are asserted.

